<div>
  <p class='text-sm font-semibold text-highlight-fg mb-2'>Nobility Tags</p>
  <div class='space-y-2 text-sm text-fg'>
    <p>
      The Nobility column of Traveller Map and T5 data is a string of single-character symbols, one per noble rank held
      on the system's main world. When a build plan loaded from either source is generated, each symbol becomes a
      <%= current_campaign ? link_to('tag', tags_path, class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2') : 'tag' %>
      on the generated main world, created in the campaign if it does not already exist. Symbols are case-sensitive;
      any symbol not listed below is ignored.
    </p>
    <table class='text-sm border-collapse'>
      <thead>
        <tr class='text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-muted border-b border-outline'>
          <th scope='col' class='pb-2 pr-8 font-semibold text-left'>Symbol</th>
          <th scope='col' class='pb-2 font-semibold text-left'>Tag</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class='divide-y divide-outline'>
        <% Tag::NOBILITY.each do |code, title| %>
          <tr>
            <td class='py-1 pr-8 text-left'><code class='text-fg-bright'><%= code %></code></td>
            <td class='py-1 text-left'><%= title %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The same symbols are used by the <code class='text-fg'>nobility</code> parameter in the
      <%= link_to 'star system specification', help_page_path('star_system_build_specification'), class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2' %>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
